+        !     rho = radial distance from optical axis (sqrt(x^2 + y^2))
+        !     Kr  = radius of curvature (NOT curvature = 1/R)
+        !     Kc  = conic constant
+        ! 
+        ! Output:
+        !     sag = z-coordinate (surface height)
+        ! 
+        ! Special cases:
+        !     Kc = 0:  Sphere
+        !     Kc = -1: Paraboloid
+        !     Kc < -1: Hyperboloid
+        !     Kc > 0:  Oblate ellipsoid
+        !     -1 < Kc < 0: Prolate ellipsoid
+        ! 
+        ! Implementation notes:
+        !     - Internally converts Kr (radius) to c (curvature) for numerical stability
+        !     - Uses curvature-based formula to avoid division by large Kr values
+        !     - Returns 0 if rho = 0 (on axis)
+        !     - Returns 0 if Kr → ∞ (flat surface)
+        !     - Returns IEEE NaN if beyond valid aperture (proper NaN handling)
+        !     - Consistent with ConSrf parameterization where Kr is radius
+        ! 
